}", "memory.md": "Closing steps. A request often ends with a closing step after the main update. Do it before you finish:
- When it ends by asking you to post a message in a Slack channel, make that post: use the channel the request names and the text it gives.
- When it ends by asking you to tag the contact, add that tag to the contact.
"}, "targets": {"worker.system_prompt": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["prompt"], "site": "agent.system_prompt"}, "worker.finish": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["prompt", "workflow"], "site": "agent.system_prompt.finish_check", "current": "Before you report the task as finished, re-read the request and check every requirement it states, including any at the end. For each one, name the tool result that shows it is done. If one is missing, do it now instead of finishing."}, "worker.stop": {"binding": "decision", "kinds": ["rule", "model"], "site": "stop.on_finish"}, "worker.harness": {"binding": "config", "kinds": ["workflow"], "site": "agent.harness_package"}}, "experience": [{"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "rejected", "installed": false, "hypothesis": "A skill the agent reads before acting, about follow-up tasks only, gets the closing task done where a line in the always-on note did not.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.0, "regression_rate": 0.0}, "reason_kinds": ["below_min_gain"]}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 2, "reused": 1, "measured": 7, "passed": 5}, {"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "rejected", "installed": false, "hypothesis": "Naming follow-up tasks in the closing-steps working note makes the agent create them, as naming posts and tags did.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.0, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 2, "reused": 0, "measured": 3, "passed": 1}, {"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "accepted", "installed": true, "hypothesis": "The agent skips closing steps its working note does not name; naming tagging in the closing-steps note fixes requests that end with a tag.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.166667, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 3, "reused": 0, "measured": 4, "passed": 1}, {"kind": "experiment", "outcome": "accepted", "installed": true, "hypothesis": "The agent skips closing Slack posts because no instruction covers them; a working note that says to make the post fixes this class of request.", "targets": ["worker.harness"], "metrics": {"gain": 0.166667, "regression_rate": 0.0}}, {"kind": "diagnosis", "noted": 1, "failures": 4, "reused": 0, "measured": 7, "passed": 3}, {"kind": "round", "outcome": "infrastructure_failed"}], "budget": {"remaining": {"usd": 44.978775}, "used": {"usd": 0.021225, "model_calls": 36.0, "input_tokens": 11955.0, "output_tokens": 1020.0}}, "notes": [{"task_id": "marketing.reh_004", "note_ref": "note:sha256:7b876b201f74f991df9ab310b9d4d200909f2c8154ede640458515d98897fdfe", "failure_class": "closing step skipped", "root_cause": "The agent made the main update and finished. The request ended with a closing step, making a named person the contact's owner, and the agent's last message says nothing in its instructions covers closing steps of this kind. The only failed check is the contact's owner.", "mechanism": "Extend the working note on closing steps: when a request ends by naming a new owner for the contact, assign that owner before finishing.", "component": "memory", "generality": "Same class as the other skipped closing steps: the agent stops after the main update whenever the closing step is of a kind its instructions do not name. Naming owner changes covers every request that ends with one."}]}
